# Title Block — საწარმოო ფურცლის წარწერა

Every architectural / structural sheet must include a title block on the
**right edge** of the sheet, framed with a thin rectangle and divided into
6 horizontal rows. Use Sylfaen Georgian font.

## Required fields (in order, top to bottom)

| Row | Field        | Georgian label   | Notes                     |
|-----|--------------|------------------|---------------------------|
| 1   | Project      | პროექტი:         | Full project name         |
| 2   | Drawing      | ნახაზი:          | Sheet content (e.g. ფუნდამენტის გეგმა) |
| 3   | Sheet code   | ფურცელი:         | e.g. კ-44, A-01, FZ-3     |
| 4   | Scale        | მასშტაბი:        | e.g. 1:50, 1:100          |
| 5   | Date         | თარიღი:          | YYYY-MM                   |
| 6   | Drawn by     | შემსრულებელი:    | Author / firm             |

## Sheet codes by drawing type

Keep the same codes used in the reference projects so files match the
existing set:

- `კ-…` reinforced concrete construction (კონსტრუქცია)
- `ა-…` / `A-…` architectural (არქიტექტურა)
- `FZ-…` ფუნქციური ზონა (functional zone, GRG)
- `MZL…`, `CZ…`, `CI…`, `CTS…`, `CVC…`, `CIR…` zoning regulation codes
  used in `19_xref_grg`
- `xref_…` external-reference base files (topo, shenobebi, gzebi,
  zonireba, gengegma, sakutreba, gantavseba, etc.)

## Standard sheet sizes (mm)

| Format | Width × Height | Use                      |
|--------|----------------|--------------------------|
| A4     |  297 ×  210    | small details            |
| A3     |  420 ×  297    | small details            |
| A2     |  594 ×  420    | apartment / small house  |
| A1     |  841 ×  594    | full floor plan          |
| A0     | 1189 ×  841    | site / GRG plans         |

When drawing in metric (mm), multiply these by 1 (everything is in mm).

## Outside-margin frame

Every sheet has 3 nested rectangles: outer trim, inner frame
(margin 600 mm), and inner content area (margin 800 mm), drawn on layer
`TITLE`.

## Title above the plan content

Above the drawing area, set a centered title in 600 mm Sylfaen, plus
a 280 mm subtitle line beneath it, both on layer `TEXT`.
